@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
 	<TEXT>
 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_BASE_ADVCIV_SOME_CHANGES_PEDIA_SR</Tag>
-		<English>[H1]K-Mod to AdvCiv Changes[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Provided by AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/developer, and non-exhaustive list of some info i'd want to display there as well, from AdvCiv's (adjust to your mod path anyways etc) C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Sid Meier's Civilization IV Beyond the Sword\Beyond the Sword\Mods\AdvCiv-SAS\_0_Common_Docs\AdvCiv_Base_Doc\manual.pdf or similar path anyways etc for manual.txt or some other AdvCiv-related sources or not anyways etc.[PARAGRAPH:1]Info below may also not be updated with latest version of the manual.pdf or similar format, view them rather at base AdvCiv's github https://github.com/f1rpo/AdvCiv or some other place that has them or/and is relevant anyways etc for latest updated content or/and more exhaustive info, this below only provides some key or excerpted info for quick view and hopefully helpful too and as i (AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/developer) wanted to, anyways etc.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Notable adjustments to K-Mod AI behavior (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc):[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- AI razes fewer cities and less randomly; 116[NEWLINE]- uses Slavery and Drafting less aggressively, though still frequently; 121b, 017[NEWLINE]- uses destructive espionage missions only against civs it dislikes; 120[NEWLINE]- will rarely found a religion before a second city (reinforcing K-Mod changes that make the AI less interested in the early religions). 171[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Reverted by AdvCiv (i (AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/developer anyways etc) assume from K-Mod (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc) (anyways etc)):[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- See Immortal Culture about reverted changes to culture and revolts.[NEWLINE]- Production overflow is never invested into an additional unit as this had lead to balance problems with AI civs training multiple Archers per turn. Instead, excess overflow is converted into gold as in the Unofficial Patch, though with some tweaks to make this conversion more difficult to abuse. 064b[NEWLINE]- Gifting Great People to the AI does not provide a relations bonus. 141[NEWLINE]- No impact of global research on inflation; instead, adjusted tech costs based on difficulty and the years-per-turn progression for a more historically accurate tech pace, and Immortal and Deity games now start on turn 10. 251, 910[NEWLINE]-  Some minor balance changes undone that weren't pulling their weight in terms of added complexity (change 200) (non-exhaustive (AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/develoepr note anyways etc)): All corporations have the same maintenance multiplier (i.e. mostly as in BtS)[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Important miscellaneous changes in AdvCiv (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc)[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- Workers and settlers only have a 50% chance of being captured and 0% if attacked on the same turn as declaring war. 010[NEWLINE]- When a tile with unfinished worker builds is left alone for more than 7 turns, the invested worker turns begin to decay. This is mainly to disincentivize pre-chopping. 011[NEWLINE]- Forest and Jungle provide only 25% defense, and none if the tile is owned by the attacker. 012[NEWLINE]- Unowned Forests and Jungles can't be chopped down. 119[NEWLINE]- The AI evacuates land units that can't defend well from cities that are about to be attacked and untenable. 139[NEWLINE]- When the AI has more happiness or health than it needs, it may refuse to accept resources in trade or may trade away its only copy of a resource. 036[NEWLINE]- Undefended cities stop "fearing for their safety" once Nationalism is discovered. 500c[NEWLINE]- Slavery base yield reduced to 24 production (from 30). 912d [NEWLINE]- The Spy unit can investigate rival cities, but (unlike in Warlords) with a mission cost. 103[NEWLINE]- Research progress toward a tech makes that tech cheaper to steal. 120i[NEWLINE]- When a citizen starves, the Granary is emptied to delay further starvation. 160[NEWLINE]- The Apostolic Palace can propose war against (non-full) voting members, but only full members are compelled to declare war. kekm.25[NEWLINE]- Can no longer bypass the Theocracy restriction by gifting missionaries. 123a/ kekm.4[NEWLINE]- Damage from nuclear weapons to units made less predictable; SDI interception chance reduced from 75% to 60% and cost increased from 1000 to 1500 production. 650[NEWLINE]- Wonders that have been manually removed from the production queue generate no "fail gold." Also no gold from national units. 123f[NEWLINE]- Trade routes can only come from revealed cities, and the paths to those cities need to be revealed as well. Cities are temporarily unavailable for trade when in disorder. Trade along rivers doesn't require any tech (as in Warlords; BtS demands Sailing). When borders of a war enemy block trade, a naval blockade can override this. Connecting a resource on an island workable by a mainland city requires only a road, not a fort. 124[NEWLINE]- When mountain peaks block off part of a landmass, the parts are treated as separate continents. This is relevant for the placement of Barbarians, colony maintenance and wonders that affect only one continent - though the main point is to make things easier for the AI. 030[NEWLINE]- Land threshold for Domination victory reduced, especially in large games. 254[NEWLINE]- On Emperor difficulty and above, some of the AI discounts have been reduced, but human civs face increased production costs, research costs, city growth thresholds and Great Person thresholds. The AI also starts with fewer freebies, in particular, without Agriculture on Immortal and Deity and without a second free Settler on Deity. Progressive AI bonuses are now based on the game turn instead of the AI era. 251/ 250e[NEWLINE]- Marathon speed is only 2.5 times slower than Normal speed, not 3 times. 252[NEWLINE]- The default player count is 8 for the Standard map size. 137[NEWLINE]- Map generation: Clusters of Gold, Gems made less common. Silver may occur on Grassland Forest. No Flood Plains on river corners. Jungle may occur on Plains. 129[NEWLINE]- New algorithm for assigning starting locations. Should partition the available land more evenly than in BtS. Not enabled for all map scripts (list). 027, 108[NEWLINE]- Switched the no-war-probability of Roosevelt and Darius, meaning that Darius can start wars when pleased, and Roosevelt - normally - cannot. 005a[NEWLINE]- Suryavarman's favorite religion is Hinduism and his favorite civic Caste System. 005a[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Other information i scraped/found (long ago (relatively) (at the start of this mod) and can finally add in AdvCiv-SAS but anyways etc...):[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:2]About the below info in this section, it comes from/in anyways etc code comments from base AdvCiv or similar that i have removed our mod (mostly from the old strategy history panel fields we don't use anymore as they are/can be inaccurate/hard to update as well but anyways etc) (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc) ; note that these below are not from base AdvCiv's manual so they may be inaccurate even more or not than manual doc added in this page (Mods Info/ Changes from K-Mod to AdvCiv) (anyways etc), anyways etc ; please also note that we don't update the [LINK=CONCEPT_ADVANCED_START]concepts pages (now in "Outdated" category in AdvCiv-SAS's sevopedia anyways etc)[\LINK] so part of the info below (at least the one related to concepts, may not apply anymore to our mod at all and is just base AdvCiv info for exhaustiveness anyways etc, as for all other info we altered some changes made by AdvCiv while we kept many or some, please view docs or/and [LINK=CONCEPT_ADVCIV_SAS_CORE_CHANGES]CONCEPT_ADVCIV_SAS_CORE_CHANGES[\LINK] for details)[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]- (AdvCiv): Defense from Walls is not cumulative with defense from city culture. The higher of the two values counts.[NEWLINE]- (AdvCiv): The defense modifier from Castle replaces the one from Wall and is not cumulative with defense from city culture[NEWLINE]- units in friendly cities and forts are safe from Flank Attacks.[NEWLINE]- SISTINE_CHAPEL (note (in anyways etc) advciv-sas anyways etc: in AdvCiv-SAS is now replaced with [LINK=BUILDING_NATYA_SHASTRA]Natya Shastra[\LINK] anyways etc and this is fixed too i.e. it now doubles after x turns like all other buildings too if i am not mistaken anyways etc even though not best place to say but at least said if i may say but anyways etc anyways etc anyways etc...) unlike other building [ICON_CULTURE] rates, the added [ICON_CULTURE] rate doesn't double after 1000 years.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_ESPIONAGE Addition: advc.132 allows switching to civics not run by the Spy owner.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_CITIES advc.004f: "We Love the King Day" disabled by AdvCiv.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_LATE_START advc.250b: Added mention of the new SPaH option and a clarification that later-era start and advanced start are separate things. Overwrites text in Civ4GameText_BTS.xml.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_UNITS  advc.010: Worker capturing has limitations; advc.005e.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_VASSAL_STATES advc.141: Pointed out change in happiness rule. Removed mention of vassal maintenance "dragging the economy to a halt"; it's not so dramatic. Vassal maint. is still mentioned.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_COMBAT and added info that feature defense depends on tile ownership.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT Added mention of Executives as special cargo.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT advc.123c: Rule change for loading units into cargo mentioned.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_DIPLOMACY Referring reader to the manual about AI refusal to talk (advc.104i) and tribute demands (advc.130o); clarified that the manner of declaring war doesn't make a difference, that tribute can't be demanded from pleased AI leaders, and that the AI doesn't normally declare war when the player declines an offer. Removed mention of "disband[ing] buildings" as this is not possible.[NEWLINE]- TXT_KEY_TRAIT_CREATIVE_PEDIA (note: advc.908b if i am not mistaken from my notes of these? Anyways etc) Since K-Mod and AdvCiv make [ICON_CULTURE] points more worthwhile in several ways, AdvCiv reduces the [ICON_CULTURE] rate (was 2 in BtS) and adds some free initial [ICON_CULTURE] instead. AdvCiv has also removed the faster [ICON_PRODUCTION] of Colosseum - which doesn't seem to fit the culture theme well. (note: advc.908b if i am not mistaken from my notes of these? Anyways etc) [NEWLINE]- _CIVIC_STATE_PROPERTY_ K-Mod treats colony maintenance as separate from distance maintenance, so this civic no longer affects colony maintenance.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_PROMOTIONS Overwrites CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts. Just correcting a bit of misinformation: When it comes to combat XP, it does matter who attacked.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_RESOURCES Overwrites CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts. Correction: Duplicate resources do have uses with BtS.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_COMBAT advc.012: Corrected two examples that say that Forest grants 50% def, Weirdly, an example in TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_TERRAIN_PEDIA already said that Forest defense is 25%. Perhaps it was changed to 50% late in development.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_ESPIONAGE [advc.103] Added note about Spies being able to investigate cities.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_FOOD [advc.160] Replaced "half" of the food with "a portion". Added mention of the Granary under "Insufficient Food".[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT advc.906: Submarine becomes Attack Submarine (note: i also added this note if i am mistaken and does not come from base AdvCiv, adding it for exhaustiveness and just in case as well, anyways etc..., anyways etc...:  advc.005e (but did not check 005e though))[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_UNITED_NATIONS advc.148: Overwriting the key in CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts.xml. AI voting behavior outlined. Victory vote was missing entirely in German.[NEWLINE]- CIV_INCA advc.004g: Dropped mention of Quechua</English>
+		<English>[H1]K-Mod to AdvCiv Changes[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Provided by AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/developer, and non-exhaustive list of some info i'd want to display there as well, from AdvCiv's (adjust to your mod path anyways etc) C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Sid Meier's Civilization IV Beyond the Sword\Beyond the Sword\Mods\AdvCiv-SAS\_0_Common_Docs\AdvCiv_Base_Doc\manual.pdf or similar path anyways etc for manual.txt or some other AdvCiv-related sources or not anyways etc.[PARAGRAPH:1]Info below may also not be updated with latest version of the manual.pdf or similar format, view them rather at base AdvCiv's github https://github.com/f1rpo/AdvCiv or some other place that has them or/and is relevant anyways etc for latest updated content or/and more exhaustive info, this below only provides some key or excerpted info for quick view.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Notable adjustments to K-Mod AI behavior (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc):[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- AI razes fewer cities and less randomly; 116[NEWLINE]- uses Slavery and Drafting less aggressively, though still frequently; 121b, 017[NEWLINE]- uses destructive espionage missions only against civs it dislikes; 120[NEWLINE]- will rarely found a religion before a second city (reinforcing K-Mod changes that make the AI less interested in the early religions). 171[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Reverted by AdvCiv (i (AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/developer anyways etc) assume from K-Mod (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc) (anyways etc)):[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- See Immortal Culture about reverted changes to culture and revolts.[NEWLINE]- Production overflow is never invested into an additional unit as this had lead to balance problems with AI civs training multiple Archers per turn. Instead, excess overflow is converted into gold as in the Unofficial Patch, though with some tweaks to make this conversion more difficult to abuse. 064b[NEWLINE]- Gifting Great People to the AI does not provide a relations bonus. 141[NEWLINE]- No impact of global research on inflation; instead, adjusted tech costs based on difficulty and the years-per-turn progression for a more historically accurate tech pace, and Immortal and Deity games now start on turn 10. 251, 910[NEWLINE]-  Some minor balance changes undone that weren't pulling their weight in terms of added complexity (change 200) (non-exhaustive (AdvCiv-SAS maintainer/develoepr note anyways etc)): All corporations have the same maintenance multiplier (i.e. mostly as in BtS)[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Important miscellaneous changes in AdvCiv (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc)[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- Workers and settlers only have a 50% chance of being captured and 0% if attacked on the same turn as declaring war. 010[NEWLINE]- When a tile with unfinished worker builds is left alone for more than 7 turns, the invested worker turns begin to decay. This is mainly to disincentivize pre-chopping. 011[NEWLINE]- Forest and Jungle provide only 25% defense, and none if the tile is owned by the attacker. 012[NEWLINE]- Unowned Forests and Jungles can't be chopped down. 119[NEWLINE]- The AI evacuates land units that can't defend well from cities that are about to be attacked and untenable. 139[NEWLINE]- When the AI has more happiness or health than it needs, it may refuse to accept resources in trade or may trade away its only copy of a resource. 036[NEWLINE]- Undefended cities stop "fearing for their safety" once Nationalism is discovered. 500c[NEWLINE]- Slavery base yield reduced to 24 production (from 30). 912d [NEWLINE]- The Spy unit can investigate rival cities, but (unlike in Warlords) with a mission cost. 103[NEWLINE]- Research progress toward a tech makes that tech cheaper to steal. 120i[NEWLINE]- When a citizen starves, the Granary is emptied to delay further starvation. 160[NEWLINE]- The Apostolic Palace can propose war against (non-full) voting members, but only full members are compelled to declare war. kekm.25[NEWLINE]- Can no longer bypass the Theocracy restriction by gifting missionaries. 123a/ kekm.4[NEWLINE]- Damage from nuclear weapons to units made less predictable; SDI interception chance reduced from 75% to 60% and cost increased from 1000 to 1500 production. 650[NEWLINE]- Wonders that have been manually removed from the production queue generate no "fail gold." Also no gold from national units. 123f[NEWLINE]- Trade routes can only come from revealed cities, and the paths to those cities need to be revealed as well. Cities are temporarily unavailable for trade when in disorder. Trade along rivers doesn't require any tech (as in Warlords; BtS demands Sailing). When borders of a war enemy block trade, a naval blockade can override this. Connecting a resource on an island workable by a mainland city requires only a road, not a fort. 124[NEWLINE]- When mountain peaks block off part of a landmass, the parts are treated as separate continents. This is relevant for the placement of Barbarians, colony maintenance and wonders that affect only one continent - though the main point is to make things easier for the AI. 030[NEWLINE]- Land threshold for Domination victory reduced, especially in large games. 254[NEWLINE]- On Emperor difficulty and above, some of the AI discounts have been reduced, but human civs face increased production costs, research costs, city growth thresholds and Great Person thresholds. The AI also starts with fewer freebies, in particular, without Agriculture on Immortal and Deity and without a second free Settler on Deity. Progressive AI bonuses are now based on the game turn instead of the AI era. 251/ 250e[NEWLINE]- Marathon speed is only 2.5 times slower than Normal speed, not 3 times. 252[NEWLINE]- The default player count is 8 for the Standard map size. 137[NEWLINE]- Map generation: Clusters of Gold, Gems made less common. Silver may occur on Grassland Forest. No Flood Plains on river corners. Jungle may occur on Plains. 129[NEWLINE]- New algorithm for assigning starting locations. Should partition the available land more evenly than in BtS. Not enabled for all map scripts (list). 027, 108[NEWLINE]- Switched the no-war-probability of Roosevelt and Darius, meaning that Darius can start wars when pleased, and Roosevelt - normally - cannot. 005a[NEWLINE]- Suryavarman's favorite religion is Hinduism and his favorite civic Caste System. 005a[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Other information i scraped/found (long ago (relatively) (at the start of this mod) and can finally add in AdvCiv-SAS but anyways etc...):[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:2]About the below info in this section, it comes from/in anyways etc code comments from base AdvCiv or similar that i have removed our mod (mostly from the old strategy history panel fields we don't use anymore as they are/can be inaccurate/hard to update as well but anyways etc) (non-exhaustive as well anyways etc) ; note that these below are not from base AdvCiv's manual so they may be inaccurate even more or not than manual doc added in this page (Mods Info/ Changes from K-Mod to AdvCiv) (anyways etc), anyways etc ; please also note that we don't update the [LINK=CONCEPT_ADVANCED_START]concepts pages (now in "Outdated" category in AdvCiv-SAS's sevopedia anyways etc)[\LINK] so part of the info below (at least the one related to concepts, may not apply anymore to our mod at all and is just base AdvCiv info for exhaustiveness anyways etc, as for all other info we altered some changes made by AdvCiv while we kept many or some, please view docs or/and [LINK=CONCEPT_ADVCIV_SAS_CORE_CHANGES]CONCEPT_ADVCIV_SAS_CORE_CHANGES[\LINK] for details)[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]- (AdvCiv): Defense from Walls is not cumulative with defense from city culture. The higher of the two values counts.[NEWLINE]- (AdvCiv): The defense modifier from Castle replaces the one from Wall and is not cumulative with defense from city culture[NEWLINE]- units in friendly cities and forts are safe from Flank Attacks.[NEWLINE]- SISTINE_CHAPEL (note (in anyways etc) advciv-sas anyways etc: in AdvCiv-SAS is now replaced with [LINK=BUILDING_NATYA_SHASTRA]Natya Shastra[\LINK] anyways etc and this is fixed too i.e. it now doubles after x turns like all other buildings too if i am not mistaken) unlike other building [ICON_CULTURE] rates, the added [ICON_CULTURE] rate doesn't double after 1000 years.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_ESPIONAGE Addition: advc.132 allows switching to civics not run by the Spy owner.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_CITIES advc.004f: "We Love the King Day" disabled by AdvCiv.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_LATE_START advc.250b: Added mention of the new SPaH option and a clarification that later-era start and advanced start are separate things. Overwrites text in Civ4GameText_BTS.xml.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_UNITS  advc.010: Worker capturing has limitations; advc.005e.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_VASSAL_STATES advc.141: Pointed out change in happiness rule. Removed mention of vassal maintenance "dragging the economy to a halt"; it's not so dramatic. Vassal maint. is still mentioned.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_COMBAT and added info that feature defense depends on tile ownership.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT Added mention of Executives as special cargo.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT advc.123c: Rule change for loading units into cargo mentioned.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_DIPLOMACY Referring reader to the manual about AI refusal to talk (advc.104i) and tribute demands (advc.130o); clarified that the manner of declaring war doesn't make a difference, that tribute can't be demanded from pleased AI leaders, and that the AI doesn't normally declare war when the player declines an offer. Removed mention of "disband[ing] buildings" as this is not possible.[NEWLINE]- TXT_KEY_TRAIT_CREATIVE_PEDIA (note: advc.908b if i am not mistaken from my notes of these? Anyways etc) Since K-Mod and AdvCiv make [ICON_CULTURE] points more worthwhile in several ways, AdvCiv reduces the [ICON_CULTURE] rate (was 2 in BtS) and adds some free initial [ICON_CULTURE] instead. AdvCiv has also removed the faster [ICON_PRODUCTION] of Colosseum - which doesn't seem to fit the culture theme well. (note: advc.908b if i am not mistaken from my notes of these? Anyways etc) [NEWLINE]- _CIVIC_STATE_PROPERTY_ K-Mod treats colony maintenance as separate from distance maintenance, so this civic no longer affects colony maintenance.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_PROMOTIONS Overwrites CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts. Just correcting a bit of misinformation: When it comes to combat XP, it does matter who attacked.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_RESOURCES Overwrites CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts. Correction: Duplicate resources do have uses with BtS.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_COMBAT advc.012: Corrected two examples that say that Forest grants 50% def, Weirdly, an example in TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_TERRAIN_PEDIA already said that Forest defense is 25%. Perhaps it was changed to 50% late in development.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_ESPIONAGE [advc.103] Added note about Spies being able to investigate cities.[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_FOOD [advc.160] Replaced "half" of the food with "a portion". Added mention of the Granary under "Insufficient Food".[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_TRANSPORT advc.906: Submarine becomes Attack Submarine (note: i also added this note if i am mistaken and does not come from base AdvCiv, adding it for exhaustiveness and just in case as well, anyways etc..., anyways etc...:  advc.005e (but did not check 005e though))[NEWLINE]- CONCEPT_UNITED_NATIONS advc.148: Overwriting the key in CIV4GameText_Civilopedia_Concepts.xml. AI voting behavior outlined. Victory vote was missing entirely in German.[NEWLINE]- CIV_INCA advc.004g: Dropped mention of Quechua</English>
 	</TEXT>
 
 
